{"files": [{"id": 38660727, "name": "ppat.1010800.g008.tif", "size": 795060, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/38660727", "supplied_md5": "aa41bb3ba4917fec6025e60eb8394649", "computed_md5": "aa41bb3ba4917fec6025e60eb8394649", "mimetype": "image/tiff"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 14305263, "full_name": "Alejandro Mat\u00eda", "first_name": "Alejandro", "last_name": "Mat\u00eda", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14305266, "full_name": "Maria M. Lorenzo", "first_name": "Maria M.", "last_name": "Lorenzo", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14305269, "full_name": "Yolimar C. Romero-Estremera", "first_name": "Yolimar C.", "last_name": "Romero-Estremera", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14305272, "full_name": "Juana M. S\u00e1nchez-Puig", "first_name": "Juana M.", "last_name": "S\u00e1nchez-Puig", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14223767, "full_name": "Angel Zaballos", "first_name": "Angel", "last_name": "Zaballos", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 468443, "full_name": "Rafael Blasco", "first_name": "Rafael", "last_name": "Blasco", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/figure/B2M_gene_inactivation_affects_VV_internalization_/21784674", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p>A) and B) HeLa and B2M KO cells were infected with V -A4-cherry at m.o.i. = 4 during 1 h at 4\u00b0C to avoid internalization. Cells were incubated for different times at 37\u00b0C and non-permeabilized cells were stained with antibody to VV-A27 (green) to visualize cell surface virus particles. White arrow-heads mark internalized virions (only red in merged image) and yellow-empty arrow-heads indicate non-internalized virions (green or yellow). Cell nucleus was labeled in blue by Hoechst staining. Internalized virions were quantified for each time point showing significant differences between HeLa and B2M KO cell lines. p-values: **** < 0.0001, *** < 0.001, ** < 0.01, * < 0.05, ns > 0.05. Scale bars: 5 \u03bcm.</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 795060, "created_date": "2022-12-27T18:42:37Z", "modified_date": "2023-06-27T10:46:37Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["wide genetic screens", "therefore cell survival", "screening top hits", "provide complete resistance", "consistently found \u03b2", "single gene knock", "significant gene hits", "early gene expression", "find genes necessary", "absolute infection blockage", "thus allow cells", "downstream related pathways", "div >< p", "vaccinia virus infection", "vaccinia virus", "b2m gene", "identify genes", "genes belonging", "survive infection", "virus internalization", "virus entry", "virus binding", "surviving cells", "significantly diminished", "results point", "relevant factor", "reduced probability", "proteins known", "powerful tools", "novel finding", "host factors", "host factor", "2 microglobulin", "&# 946"], "keywords": ["wide genetic screens", "therefore cell survival", "screening top hits", "provide complete resistance", "consistently found \u03b2", "single gene knock", "significant gene hits", "early gene expression", "find genes necessary", "absolute infection blockage", "thus allow cells", "downstream related pathways", "div >< p", "vaccinia virus infection", "vaccinia virus", "b2m gene", "identify genes", "genes belonging", "survive infection", "virus internalization", "virus entry", "virus binding", "surviving cells", "significantly diminished", "results point", "relevant factor", "reduced probability", "proteins known", "powerful tools", "novel finding", "h